# Base URL of a real eShopOnWeb PublicApi instance (see eshoponweb-siva:
# docs/as_is_lld/as_is_lld_catalog.md, Section 11 for the full API contract).
#
# Leave this UNSET for local development: the app falls back to its own
# built-in mock endpoints (src/app/api/*, seeded from eshoponweb-siva's
# real CatalogContextSeed.cs data - see src/mocks/) so the catalog screen
# works out of the box with no backend running. See src/lib/getApiBaseUrl.ts.
#
# Local .NET dev default, once you want to point at the real backend
# (src/PublicApi/appsettings.json -> baseUrls.apiBase):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://localhost:5099/api/

# NOTE: PublicApi's CORS policy allows exactly one configured origin
# (baseUrls:webBase in the API's appsettings). This app's origin must be
# set there once you point at a real backend - the built-in mock endpoints
# above are same-origin and unaffected by this.
